\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The concept is well described. It's an interesting strategy of supply chain based pairs trading. The performance is not ideal.\'a0\
Here's my suggestions to improve it:\
1. It is unclear that which commodity future you are using. I reviewed the code but couldn't find the commodity tickers.\'a0\
Based on different industries, operating strategies, inventories and demands, companies are using futures to hedge their costs of raw materials. You could try different futures such as 3M. 6M. 1Y, 3Y, etc.\
e.g., If a company applied a hedging strategy of futures between 3M and 6M, the company is expecting a nearly fixed price of the commodity within 6M. Therefore, 1Y future price may affect more to the stock price.\
2. The impact of commodity price changes on stock prices may appear with a multi-month lag. For example, you could pair the current 6-month futures price with a 12-month lagged stock price.\
3. I developed a similar strategy for steel industry before. I picked one steelmaker and one automaker stocks. It showed a high correlation with 3 months lagged window.\'a0\
If we assume all the companies will do future hedging, it will be hard for you to find the relations between commodities and stocks given a 5-90 day window.\
There are two ways to proceed from here: expand the time window to capture longer-term effects, or introduce an intermediate stock. For example, lumber \uc0\u8594  WFG \u8594  LEN. The correlation between WFG and LEN may be stronger.}